stateDiagram-v2
    %% One WebSocket client's lifecycle on /api/stream, and the hub
    %% backpressure contract that governs it (api/ws.go, hub/hub.go).

    [*] --> Subscribing

    Subscribing --> Accepting : Hub.Subscribe(256) BEFORE the handshake
    note right of Subscribing
        Subscribing first is deliberate: once the
        handshake completes the client can fetch
        GET /api/state knowing every subsequent
        publication already reaches this socket.
    end note

    Accepting --> Live : websocket.Accept ok
    Accepting --> Closed : handshake failed -> unsubscribe

    state Live {
        [*] --> Idle
        Idle --> Writing : event received on the subscriber chan
        Writing --> Idle : JSON frame written
        Idle --> Reading : client frame received
        Reading --> Dispatching : clientCmd decoded
        Dispatching --> Idle : ack / error / history_result written
        Idle --> Pinging : ping ticker fires
        Pinging --> Idle : pong received
    }

    Live --> Overflowed : Publish found this subscriber's<br/>256-slot buffer full
    note right of Overflowed
        The event is dropped for this subscriber only
        and its overflow chan is closed exactly once.
        A dropped event means the client can no longer
        be trusted to hold a consistent view.
    end note

    Overflowed --> Closed : writer cancels the conn ctx,<br/>socket torn down
    Live --> Closed : client close, ping timeout,<br/>read error, or server shutdown
    Closed --> Resync : client reconnects
    Resync --> Subscribing : fresh Subscribe + GET /api/state snapshot
    Closed --> [*] : unsubscribe, chan closed
